<td style="width:48%; text-align:left; border-style:none"><b>Pts:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikola_Jokić" title="Nikola Jokić">Nikola Jokić</a> 41<br/><b>Rebs:</b> Nikola Jokić 11<br/><b>Asts:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamal_Murray" title="Jamal Murray">Jamal Murray</a> 10</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="text-align:center; border-style:none"><i><b>Series tied, 1–1</b></i></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<table style="background-color:#eee; color:#202122; float:right; width:24%; table-layout:fixed">
<tbody><tr><td style="border-style:none"><div style="font-size:85%"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball_Arena" title="Ball Arena">Ball Arena</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denver,_Colorado" title="Denver, Colorado" class="mw-redirect">Denver, Colorado</a><br/><b>Attendance:</b> 19,537<br/><b>Referees:</b> 
<ul><li>No. 15 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zach_Zarba" title="Zach Zarba">Zach Zarba</a></li>
<li>No. 10 John Goble</li>
<li>No. 61 Courtney Kirkland</li></ul></div></td></tr>
</tbody></table><div style="clear:both"></div></div>
<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAfA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Heat_Duncan_Robinson_(cropped).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAfE"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Heat_Duncan_Robinson_(cropped).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Heat_Duncan_Robinson_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Heat_Duncan_Robinson_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Heat_Duncan_Robinson_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Heat_Duncan_Robinson_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2489" data-file-height="3498" data-file-type="bitmap" height="253" width="180" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAfI"/></a><figcaption id="mwAfM">The Heat opened the fourth quarter on a 15–2 run, with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duncan_Robinson_(basketball)" title="Duncan Robinson (basketball)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAfQ">Duncan Robinson</a> going 4-for-4 to help Miami regain the lead.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAfU">Miami rallied from a 15-point deficit to win 111–108 behind 23 points from Vincent and 21 each from Butler and Adebayo, becoming the first No. 8 seed to win an NBA Finals game on the road. The Heat built an early 21–10 lead with 4:56 left in the opening quarter before the Nuggets went on a 40–14 run over the next 12 minutes, turning the double-digit deficit into a double-digit lead. Down by eight entering the fourth quarter, the Heat outscored Denver 32–12 in the opening 8:21 of the fourth quarter to take a 12-point lead, then frittered most of it away and had to survive a 3-point try by Murray that missed as time expired.<sup about="#mwt145" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reynolds_Game2_37-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reynolds_Game2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-reynolds_Game2-37"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reynolds_Game2-37" id="mwAfY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfg">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfk">]</span></span></a></sup> Miami knocked down 17 of their 35 threes and converted 18 of 20 free throws after making just two in Game 1. Jokić scored a game-high 41 points but recorded a playoff-low four assists as the Nuggets lost their first home game since March 30.<sup about="#mwt146" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reynolds_Game2_37-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reynolds_Game2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reynolds_Game2-37" id="mwAfo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfw">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAf0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAf4">With Martin dealing with an illness, Miami elected to insert <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kevin_Love" title="Kevin Love" id="mwAf8">Kevin Love</a>, who did not play in Game 1, into the starting lineup.<sup about="#mwt147" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reynolds_Game2_37-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reynolds_Game2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reynolds_Game2-37" id="mwAgA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgI">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgM">]</span></span></a></sup> Strus, who was 0 for 10 in Game 1, had four 3-pointers in the first quarter as the Heat jumped out to an early 11-point lead, but the Nuggets reclaimed momentum early in the second quarter with four 3-pointers in a 70-second span as Miami trailed by as much as 15 in the first half.<sup about="#mwt148" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reynolds_Game2_37-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reynolds_Game2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reynolds_Game2-37" id="mwAgQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgY">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgc">]</span></span></a></sup> Despite an 18-point third quarter from Jokić, the Heat hung around to trail by eight entering the fourth quarter. Coming into the game, Denver was undefeated in the playoffs when leading by double digits and boasted a 37–1 record for the season when leading by at least eight points going into the final quarter.<sup about="#mwt149" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reynolds_Game2_37-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reynolds_Game2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reynolds_Game2-37" id="mwAgg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgo">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAgw">Miami opened the first 2:43 of the fourth quarter with a 15–2 scoring run, highlighted by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duncan_Robinson_(basketball)" title="Duncan Robinson (basketball)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAg0">Duncan Robinson</a> going 4 for 4 from the field to give the Heat their first lead of the second half. Miami managed to build a 12-point advantage with under 3:30 remaining but had to weather a late surge from the Nuggets, who cut the lead to three with 35 seconds remaining. After a missed 3-pointer from Butler, Denver chose not to call a timeout in the closing seconds. Murray attempted a last-second 3-point shot that could have tied the game, but it fell short. Murray finished with 18 points and 10 assists, while Jokić converted 16 of his 28 field goals as the Nuggets dropped to 0–3 this postseason when Jokić scores 40 or more points.<sup about="#mwt152" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-38" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-38"}}'><a href="#cite_note-38" id="mwAg4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAg8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhA">[</span>38<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt153" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAhI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"clear","href":"./Template:Clear"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwAhM" aria-labelledby="Game_3"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Game_3">Game 3</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2023_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Game 3"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt154" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAhQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Basketballbox","href":"./Template:Basketballbox"},"params":{"bg":{"wt":"#eee"},"date":{"wt":"June 7"},"time":{"wt":"8:30 pm"},"place":{"wt":"[[Kaseya Center]], [[Miami, Florida]]"},"TV":{"wt":"[[NBA on ABC|ABC]]"},"team1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;[[Denver Nuggets]]&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"score1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;109&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"team2":{"wt":"[[Miami Heat]]"},"score2":{"wt":"94"},"report":{"wt":"[https://www.nba.com/game/den-vs-mia-0042200403 Recap]"},"Q1":{"wt":"24–24"},"Q2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;29&apos;&apos;&apos;–24"},"Q3":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;29&apos;&apos;&apos;–20"},"Q4":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;27&apos;&apos;&apos;–26"},"points1":{"wt":"[[Jamal Murray]] 34"},"points2":{"wt":"[[Jimmy Butler]] 28"},"rebounds1":{"wt":"[[Nikola Jokić]] 21"},"rebounds2":{"wt":"[[Bam Adebayo]] 17"},"assist1":{"wt":"Jokić, Murray 10 each"},"assist2":{"wt":"[[Kyle Lowry|Lowry]], [[Max Strus|Strus]] 5 each"},"attendance":{"wt":"20,019"},"referee":{"wt":"*No. 25 [[Tony Brothers]]\n*No. 58 Josh Tiven\n*No. 24 Kevin Scott"},"series":{"wt":"Denver leads series, 2–1"}},"i":0}}]}'></div><div style="width: 100%; background-color:#eee; color:#202122;" about="#mwt154" id="mwAhU">
