</td></tr>
<tr style="vertical-align:top; font-size:85%"><td style="text-align:center; border-style:none" colspan="3"><b>Scoring by quarter:</b> 20–<b>21</b>, <b>35</b>–30, <b>31</b>–22, 22–22</td></tr><tr style="vertical-align:top; font-size:85%">
<td style="width:48%; text-align:right; border-style:none"><b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Point_(basketball)" title="Point (basketball)" class="mw-redirect">Pts</a>:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_Gordon" title="Aaron Gordon">Aaron Gordon</a> 27<br/><b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebound_(basketball)" title="Rebound (basketball)">Rebs</a>:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikola_Jokić" title="Nikola Jokić">Nikola Jokić</a> 12<br/><b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assist_(basketball)" title="Assist (basketball)">Asts</a>:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamal_Murray" title="Jamal Murray">Jamal Murray</a> 12</td>
<td></td>
<td style="width:48%; text-align:left; border-style:none"><b>Pts:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimmy_Butler" title="Jimmy Butler">Jimmy Butler</a> 25<br/><b>Rebs:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bam_Adebayo" title="Bam Adebayo">Bam Adebayo</a> 11<br/><b>Asts:</b> Butler, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyle_Lowry" title="Kyle Lowry">Lowry</a> 7 each</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="text-align:center; border-style:none"><i><b>Denver leads series, 3–1</b></i></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<table style="background-color:#eee; color:#202122; float:right; width:24%; table-layout:fixed">
<tbody><tr><td style="border-style:none"><div style="font-size:85%"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaseya_Center" title="Kaseya Center">Kaseya Center</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miami,_Florida" title="Miami, Florida" class="mw-redirect">Miami, Florida</a><br/><b>Attendance:</b> 20,184<br/><b>Referees:</b> 
<ul><li>No. 48 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scott_Foster_(basketball)" title="Scott Foster (basketball)">Scott Foster</a></li>
<li>No. 60 James Williams</li>
<li>No. 55 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Kennedy_(referee)" title="Bill Kennedy (referee)">Bill Kennedy</a></li></ul></div></td></tr>
</tbody></table><div style="clear:both"></div></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAkk"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Aaron_Gordon_2019_(cropped).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAko"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Aaron_Gordon_2019_(cropped).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Aaron_Gordon_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Aaron_Gordon_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Aaron_Gordon_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Aaron_Gordon_2019_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1039" data-file-height="1372" data-file-type="bitmap" height="251" width="190" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 0.75" id="mwAks"/></a><figcaption id="mwAkw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_Gordon" title="Aaron Gordon" id="mwAk0">Aaron Gordon</a>'s 27 points helped the Nuggets prevent a comeback attempt by the Heat to take a 3–1 series lead.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAk4">Gordon dropped a game-high 27 points on 11 of 15 from the field, Jokić chipped in 23 points and 12 rebounds, and Murray recorded 15 points and 12 assists as the Nuggets took a commanding 3–1 series lead back to Denver.<sup about="#mwt175" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reynold_06102023_43-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reynold_06102023"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-reynold_06102023-43"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reynold_06102023-43" id="mwAk8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlE">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlI">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Brown_(basketball)" title="Bruce Brown (basketball)" id="mwAlM">Bruce Brown</a> came off the bench and scored 11 of his 21 points in the fourth quarter, thwarting any attempt by the Heat to overcome their eighth double-digit deficit of the playoffs. The Nuggets won their fifth straight road game,<sup about="#mwt176" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reynold_06102023_43-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reynold_06102023"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reynold_06102023-43" id="mwAlQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlY">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlc">]</span></span></a></sup> improving to 9–1 in their last ten playoff games, while Miami dropped to 2–6 in their last eight games,<sup about="#mwt179" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-44" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-44"}}'><a href="#cite_note-44" id="mwAlg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlo">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAls">]</span></span></a></sup> as they fell into a 3–1 hole for the third consecutive finals appearance.<sup about="#mwt180" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reynold_06102023_43-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reynold_06102023"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reynold_06102023-43" id="mwAlw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAl0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAl4">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAl8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAmA">After neither team could claim a double-digit lead in the first half for the second consecutive game, the Nuggets led by 13 going into the fourth quarter. Similar to their game 2 victory, the Heat scored the first eight points of the quarter, and Jokić committed his fifth foul and had to go to the bench with 9:24 left.<sup about="#mwt181" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reynold_06102023_43-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reynold_06102023"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reynold_06102023-43" id="mwAmE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmM">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Miami narrowed the lead to five with 8:42 remaining,<sup about="#mwt182" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reynold_06102023_43-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reynold_06102023"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reynold_06102023-43" id="mwAmU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmc">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmg">]</span></span></a></sup> but the Nuggets held firm, as Brown scored 11 points during a 14–4 run down the stretch that gave Denver a 17-point lead, their largest of the night.<sup about="#mwt185" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-45" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-45"}}'><a href="#cite_note-45" id="mwAmk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAms">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmw">]</span></span></a></sup> Murray, who committed seven turnovers in game 3, finished the game with 12 assists and zero turnovers, joining <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_Johnson" title="Magic Johnson" id="mwAm0">Magic Johnson</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Reid_(basketball)" title="Robert Reid (basketball)" id="mwAm4">Robert Reid</a> as the only players to record 12-plus assists with zero turnovers in a finals game.<sup about="#mwt188" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-46" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-46"}}'><a href="#cite_note-46" id="mwAm8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnE">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAnM">Butler led the Heat with 25 points, seven rebounds, and seven assists, while Adebayo had 20 points, 11 rebounds, and seven turnovers.<sup about="#mwt189" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-reynold_06102023_43-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"reynold_06102023"}}'><a href="#cite_note-reynold_06102023-43" id="mwAnQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnY">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnc">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyle_Lowry" title="Kyle Lowry" id="mwAng">Kyle Lowry</a> chipped in with 13 points and seven assists off the bench, but the starting backcourt of Strus and Vincent scored just two points on 1 of 10 shooting as the Heat were held to under 100 points for the third time this series.<sup about="#mwt192" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-47" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-47"}}'><a href="#cite_note-47" id="mwAnk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAno"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAns">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnw">]</span></span></a></sup> The Nuggets made 14 of their 28 3-pointers, while Miami shot just 32% from deep and committed 15 turnovers after having just four in game 3.<sup about="#mwt195" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-48" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-48"}}'><a href="#cite_note-48" id="mwAn0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAn4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAn8">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoA">]</span></span></a></sup> Jokić and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kentavious_Caldwell-Pope" title="Kentavious Caldwell-Pope" id="mwAoE">Kentavious Caldwell-Pope</a> combined for six steals and five blocks, while the entire Heat team finished with just two steals and three blocks. Jokić also became the first player in NBA history to put up at least 500 points, 250 rebounds, and 150 assists in a single postseason run.<sup about="#mwt198" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-49" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-49"}}'><a href="#cite_note-49" id="mwAoI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoQ">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt199" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAoY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"clear","href":"./Template:Clear"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwAoc" aria-labelledby="Game_5"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Game_5">Game 5</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2023_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: Game 5"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div style="clear:both;" class="" about="#mwt200" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAog" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Basketballbox","href":"./Template:Basketballbox"},"params":{"bg":{"wt":"#eee"},"date":{"wt":"June 12"},"time":{"wt":"8:30 pm {{small|(6:30 pm [[Mountain Time Zone|MDT]])}}"},"place":{"wt":"[[Ball Arena]], [[Denver, Colorado]]"},"TV":{"wt":"[[NBA on ABC|ABC]]"},"team1":{"wt":"[[Miami Heat]]"},"score1":{"wt":"89"},"team2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;[[Denver Nuggets]]&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"score2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;94&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"report":{"wt":"[https://www.nba.com/game/mia-vs-den-0042200405 Recap]"},"Q1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;24&apos;&apos;&apos;–22"},"Q2":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;&apos;27&apos;&apos;&apos;–22"},"Q3":{"wt":"20–&apos;&apos;&apos;26&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"Q4":{"wt":"18–&apos;&apos;&apos;24&apos;&apos;&apos;"},"points1":{"wt":"[[Jimmy Butler]] 21"},"points2":{"wt":"[[Nikola Jokić]] 28"},"rebounds1":{"wt":"[[Bam Adebayo]] 12"},"rebounds2":{"wt":"Nikola Jokić 16"},"assist1":{"wt":"Jimmy Butler 5"},"assist2":{"wt":"[[Jamal Murray]] 8"},"attendance":{"wt":"19,537"},"referee":{"wt":"*No. 8 Marc Davis\n*No. 16 David Guthrie\n*No. 58 Josh Tiven"},"series":{"wt":"Denver wins NBA Finals, 4–1"}},"i":0}}]}'></div><div style="width: 100%; background-color:#eee; color:#202122;" about="#mwt200" id="mwAok">
