</tbody></table>
<table style="background-color:#eee; color:#202122; float:right; width:24%; table-layout:fixed">
<tbody><tr><td style="border-style:none"><div style="font-size:85%"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball_Arena" title="Ball Arena">Ball Arena</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denver,_Colorado" title="Denver, Colorado" class="mw-redirect">Denver, Colorado</a><br/><b>Attendance:</b> 19,537<br/><b>Referees:</b> 
<ul><li>No. 8 Marc Davis</li>
<li>No. 16 David Guthrie</li>
<li>No. 58 Josh Tiven</li></ul></div></td></tr>
</tbody></table><div style="clear:both"></div></div>
<figure class="mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAoo"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Nikola_Jokic_free_throw_(cropped).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAos"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Nikola_Jokic_free_throw_(cropped).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Nikola_Jokic_free_throw_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Nikola_Jokic_free_throw_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Nikola_Jokic_free_throw_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Nikola_Jokic_free_throw_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="948" data-file-height="1291" data-file-type="bitmap" height="252" width="185" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAow"/></a><figcaption id="mwAo0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikola_Jokić" title="Nikola Jokić" id="mwAo4">Nikola Jokić</a> was awarded Finals MVP, becoming the first center to win the award since <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shaquille_O'Neal" title="Shaquille O'Neal" id="mwAo8">Shaquille O'Neal</a> in 2002.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwApA">In a closely contested Game 5, Jokić propelled the Nuggets to their first NBA championship in franchise history with a hard-fought 94–89 victory over the Heat. His dominant performance, including 28 points and 16 rebounds, earned him the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_Finals_Most_Valuable_Player_Award" title="NBA Finals Most Valuable Player Award" class="mw-redirect" id="mwApE">Finals MVP award</a>.<sup about="#mwt203" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReynoldsGame5_50-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReynoldsGame5"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50" id="mwApI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApQ">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApU">]</span></span></a></sup> He became the lowest-selected player to ever win Finals MVP, being the 41st pick of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_NBA_draft" title="2014 NBA draft" id="mwApY">2014 NBA draft</a>.<sup about="#mwt206" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-51"}}'><a href="#cite_note-51" id="mwApc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApk">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApo">]</span></span></a></sup> The Nuggets struggled with their shooting throughout the game, particularly from beyond the arc, as they missed 20 of their first 22 three-point attempts;<sup about="#mwt207" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReynoldsGame5_50-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReynoldsGame5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50" id="mwAps"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp0">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp4">]</span></span></a></sup> however, Jokic's efficient 12 of 16 shooting from the field provided a much-needed boost, as he was the only starter across both teams to shoot over 50% from the field.<sup about="#mwt208" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReynoldsGame5_50-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReynoldsGame5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50" id="mwAp8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqE">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqI">]</span></span></a></sup> Jokić, who averaged 30 points, 13.5 rebounds, and 9.5 assists throughout the playoffs, became the first player in NBA history to lead the league in points (600), rebounds (269), and assists (190) in a single postseason.<sup about="#mwt209" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReynoldsGame5_50-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReynoldsGame5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50" id="mwAqM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqU">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAqc">Prior to the game, Miami announced that <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyler_Herro" title="Tyler Herro" id="mwAqg">Tyler Herro</a> was listed as active for the first time since he broke his hand in the first round against the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milwaukee_Bucks" title="Milwaukee Bucks" id="mwAqk">Milwaukee Bucks</a>.<sup about="#mwt212" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HerroGame5_52-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HerroGame5"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HerroGame5-52"}}'><a href="#cite_note-HerroGame5-52" id="mwAqo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqw">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAq0">]</span></span></a></sup> The Heat trailed by eight early in the first quarter, but a 31–13 run by Miami turned the deficit into a 10-point lead, their largest since Game 2.<sup about="#mwt215" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-53" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-53"}}'><a href="#cite_note-53" id="mwAq4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAq8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArA">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArE">]</span></span></a></sup> Adebayo scored 18 of his 20 points in the first half to give the Heat their first halftime lead of the series.<sup about="#mwt218" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NJL_54-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NJL"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NJL-54"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NJL-54" id="mwArI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArQ">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArU">]</span></span></a></sup> The Nuggets, who entered the game with a series shooting average of 37.6% from three-point range, shot a historically poor 6.7% from three-point range in the first half.<sup about="#mwt219" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReynoldsGame5_50-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReynoldsGame5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50" id="mwArY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArg">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArk">]</span></span></a></sup> Additionally, Denver committed 10 turnovers in the first half and missed 10 of their first 19 free throws.<sup about="#mwt220" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReynoldsGame5_50-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReynoldsGame5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50" id="mwAro"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArw">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAr0">]</span></span></a></sup> Despite their shooting struggles, the Nuggets showed their resiliency, as they stormed back to take an 83–76 lead with 4:43 left in the fourth quarter.<sup about="#mwt221" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NJL_54-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NJL"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NJL-54" id="mwAr4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAr8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsA">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAsI">Butler, who made just two field goals in the first 43 minutes of the game, scored 13 consecutive points for Miami to give them a one-point lead with two minutes to go;<sup about="#mwt222" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReynoldsGame5_50-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReynoldsGame5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50" id="mwAsM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsU">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsY">]</span></span></a></sup> however, an offensive rebound and tip-in by Brown swung the momentum back in favor of the Nuggets. After a steal and two free throws from Pope, Butler missed a contested 3-pointer and Brown hit free throws in the final seconds to seal the win for Denver.<sup about="#mwt223" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReynoldsGame5_50-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReynoldsGame5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50" id="mwAsc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsk">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAso">]</span></span></a></sup> Murray contributed 14 points, eight rebounds, and eight assists, while Porter Jr. recorded 16 points and 13 rebounds for the Nuggets.<sup about="#mwt224" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NJL_54-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NJL"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NJL-54" id="mwAss"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAs0">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAs4">]</span></span></a></sup> Butler finished with 21 points on 5 for 18 from the field for the Heat, and Adebayo recorded his fourth 20-point double-double of the series.<sup about="#mwt225" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReynoldsGame5_50-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReynoldsGame5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50" id="mwAs8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtE">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtI">]</span></span></a></sup> Although Herro was listed as available, coach <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erik_Spoelstra" title="Erik Spoelstra" id="mwAtM">Erik Spoelstra</a> elected not to play him.<sup about="#mwt226" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HerroGame5_52-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HerroGame5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-HerroGame5-52" id="mwAtQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtY">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtc">]</span></span></a></sup> Miami's shooting woes ultimately proved costly, as they shot an inadequate 26% from three-point range and 34% from the field, their lowest percentage of the season.<sup about="#mwt227" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReynoldsGame5_50-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReynoldsGame5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50" id="mwAtg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAto">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAts">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAtw">Denver became the second original <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Basketball_Association" title="American Basketball Association" id="mwAt0">ABA</a> franchise, along with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Antonio_Spurs" title="San Antonio Spurs" id="mwAt4">San Antonio Spurs</a>, to win an NBA championship.<sup about="#mwt228" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReynoldsGame5_50-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReynoldsGame5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReynoldsGame5-50" id="mwAt8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuE">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuI">]</span></span></a></sup> It was the Nuggets' first league championship after 56 combined years in the ABA and NBA.<sup about="#mwt231" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-55" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-55"}}'><a href="#cite_note-55" id="mwAuM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuU">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuY">]</span></span></a></sup> Denver was also the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Conference_(NBA)" title="Western Conference (NBA)" id="mwAuc">Western Conference</a> team from outside the states of California or Texas to win the championship since the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1978–79_Seattle_SuperSonics_season" title="1978–79 Seattle SuperSonics season" id="mwAug">1978–79 Seattle SuperSonics</a>.<sup about="#mwt234" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-56" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-56"}}'><a href="#cite_note-56" id="mwAuk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAus">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuw">]</span></span></a></sup> This was the final game of Haslem's NBA career, as he retired the following month.<sup about="#mwt237" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-57" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-57"}}'><a href="#cite_note-57" id="mwAu0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAu4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAu8">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwAvE" aria-labelledby="Rosters"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Rosters">Rosters</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2023_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: Rosters"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
